+# ADR-0127 — Root-owned single-object reclamation
+
+Status: Draft implementation and qualification; Internal M8 scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+Expose permanent removal through an independently presented Root chooser and
+physical confirmation. Ordinary Files namespace authority continues to offer
+reversible Trash/Restore only. There is no new public File privilege, Kernel
+authority, mapping, capability, resource budget or global privilege toggle.
+
+Root lists the actual Workspace Dataset through its held role16 control route.
+The decision freezes the exact dataset, object generation/revision, namespace
+revision and name. Normal presentation shows name, size/location, retirement of
+existing access and permanent loss of Restore; L3 exposes diagnostic identities.
+Directory removal is limited to one directly trashed empty directory. No subtree
+is recursively collected. Original volumes, Root/private namespaces and raw
+storage selectors are outside this operation.
+
+## Custody and admission
+
+Before confirmation, Root drains its own Inspector metadata stream under one
+retained drain cut. An external semantic session, pending owner action, queued
+controls or uncertain Display owner refuses entry. App/semantic messages cannot
+confirm this workflow. A real completed protected frame, actual Input barrier
+and fresh physical gesture produce the single-use scoped effect.
+
+After confirmation, one original absolute cut covers the entire workflow. Root
+blocks new binding and ordinary controls while preserving the sole accepted
+owner. For each matching installed File lease, it uses the independently held
+ProcessCONTROL and exact issued44 nonce with Kernel61. Only actual Drained or
+the exact existing never-enqueued receipt permits service reconciliation.
+Logical revoke, release ACK and a timer do not return an accepted loan. Unrelated
+leases and private application copies remain owned by their existing owners.
+
+One additive Root-only Purge command uses the existing role16/window503 control
+transport. Its fields are descriptive correlation, not a ReclaimFence proof.
+The service independently rejects active or unretired matching File routes,
+namespace bindings fixed to the target, pending requests, transfer/staging or
+verification, poisoned or unmirrored storage, shutdown seals and uncertain
+transport. It rechecks the complete object/name/revision/namespace CAS before
+assigning its own durable operation ID and retaining the original request.
+
+The existing Dataset purge publishes and verifies mirrored metadata. Applied is
+returned only with the exact Purged receipt and actual allocation counts. Root
+also validates the exact response and original cut. A timeout, malformed reply,
+late actual result or unknown I/O retains the request, old facts and owners;
+it does not retry, renew the cut, advertise free space or silently clear debt.
+There is no use of terminal shutdown Quiesce, which would prohibit later reuse.
+
+Vacant slots retain generation; later Create increments it. A stale object cannot
+address a replacement. Trash and other retained catalog entries remain allocation
+roots until an independently authorized permanent removal. Cold orphan-stage
+cleanup and general compaction remain separate unsupported operations.
+
+## Qualification
+
+Retain host refusal/cut/publication tests, strict host and native checks, actual
+linked ELF/census and source pins, then owned native UI purge/Create/reuse and
+cold exact-byte evidence. Model checks or a supplied fence epoch alone do not
+establish native retirement, persistence, eligible free space or M8 acceptance.
